{"arrivo":"uk","origine":"zlw-opl","origine_nome":"Old Polish","livello2":"zlw-ocs","livello2_nome":"Old Czech","n":6,"parole":[{"parola":"дотеп","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"sì","motivo_incerta":"Possibly; Probably","significato":"wisecrack, quip, witticism, repartee, pun","termine_origine":"dowcip","catena":[{"codice":"zlw-opl","nome":"Old Polish","termine":"dowcip","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"zlw-ocs","nome":"Old Czech","termine":"dovtip","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"sla-pro","nome":"Proto-Slavic","termine":"*těpati","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"sla-pro","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Inherited from Old Ruthenian довтепъ (dovtep), probably from Old Polish dowcip, ultimately from Old Czech dovtip, possibly from Proto-Slavic *těpati. Forms such as Old Ruthenian довципъ (dovcip) were definitely borrowed from Polish."},{"parola":"пиха","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"arrogance, haughtiness, conceit, hubris","termine_origine":"pycha","catena":[{"codice":"zlw-opl","nome":"Old Polish","termine":"pycha","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"zlw-ocs","nome":"Old Czech","termine":"pýcha","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"sla-pro","nome":"Proto-Slavic","termine":"*pyxati","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"sla-pro","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Inherited from Old Ruthenian пыха, пиха (pyxa, pixa), from Old Polish pycha, from Old Czech pýcha, deverbal from Old Czech pýchati, from Proto-Slavic *pyxati (“to puff”). For an identical development compare Ukrainian наду́тий (nadútyj), Russian надме́нный, наду́тый (nadménnyj, nadútyj)."},{"parola":"праця","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"work, labor","termine_origine":"praca","catena":[{"codice":"zlw-opl","nome":"Old Polish","termine":"praca","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"zlw-ocs","nome":"Old Czech","termine":"prácě","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"sla-pro","nome":"Proto-Slavic","termine":"*porťa","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"sla-pro","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Inherited from Old Ruthenian пра́ца (práca), from Old Polish praca, from Old Czech prácě, from Proto-Slavic *porťa."},{"parola":"рада","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"council","termine_origine":"rada","catena":[{"codice":"zlw-opl","nome":"Old Polish","termine":"rada","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"zlw-ocs","nome":"Old Czech","termine":"rada","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"gmh","nome":"Middle High German","termine":"rāt","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"gmw-pro","nome":"Proto-West Germanic","termine":"*rād","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"gem-pro","nome":"Proto-Germanic","termine":"*rēdaz","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"gem-pro","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Inherited from Old Ruthenian ра́да (ráda), from Old East Slavic ра́да (ráda), from Old Polish rada, from Old Czech rada, from Middle High German rāt, from Old High German rāt, from Proto-West Germanic *rād, from Proto-Germanic *rēdaz."},{"parola":"смертельний","pos":"adj","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"deadly, lethal, fatal, mortal (resulting in death)","termine_origine":"śmiertelny","catena":[{"codice":"zlw-opl","nome":"Old Polish","termine":"śmiertelny","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"zlw-ocs","nome":"Old Czech","termine":"smrtedlný","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"zlw-ocs","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Inherited from Old Ruthenian смерте́льный (smertélʹnyj), from Old Polish śmiertelny, ultimately from Old Czech smrtedlný."},{"parola":"спосіб","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"sì","motivo_incerta":"Possibly","significato":"way, means, manner","termine_origine":"sposób","catena":[{"codice":"zlw-opl","nome":"Old Polish","termine":"sposób","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"zlw-ocs","nome":"Old Czech","termine":"zpósob","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"sla-pro","nome":"Proto-Slavic","termine":"*sъposobъ","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"sla-pro","ambiti":["scienza"],"via":"","testo":"Inherited from Old Ruthenian спо́собъ (spósob), most likely from Old Polish sposób, which itself is possibly from Old Czech zpósob (maybe only influenced semantically), from Proto-Slavic *sъposobъ."}]}